1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,779
Welcome to Rez grid Academy.

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:06,019
In this lesson, we will configure
a department and protect access.

3
00:00:06,489 --> 00:00:10,970
Wrong time zones distort schedules,
and broad permissions expose work

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,600
to people who do not need it.

5
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:16,340
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,299
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:22,199
An administrator sets the department
time zone, hides modules the

8
00:00:22,199 --> 00:00:26,450
department will not use, requires
two-factor sign-in for administrators

9
00:00:26,679 --> 00:00:28,750
and adds a second administrator.

10
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:33,769
Sets the time zone and address everything
else uses, and keeps administrative

11
00:00:33,809 --> 00:00:35,670
access limited and recoverable.

12
00:00:36,229 --> 00:00:39,680
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

13
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,900
scenarios, not default settings.

14
00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:43,249
Department Settings.

15
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,770
Department address, time
zone and core settings.

16
00:00:47,259 --> 00:00:52,130
Confirm the address and time zone;
dates, maps and schedules depend on them.

17
00:00:52,349 --> 00:00:53,420
Module settings.

18
00:00:53,859 --> 00:00:57,240
Turn optional modules on
or off for the department.

19
00:00:57,660 --> 00:01:01,160
Hide modules you will not use
so members see a simpler menu.

20
00:01:01,469 --> 00:01:02,240
Permissions.

21
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,800
Who can create calls, see
personal information and

22
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,720
perform other sensitive actions.

23
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:11,599
Review each permission; some
default to every member.

24
00:01:11,839 --> 00:01:13,490
Two-Factor Authentication.

25
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:16,169
Two-factor sign-in for member accounts.

26
00:01:16,569 --> 00:01:19,640
Enroll every administrator
in two-factor sign-in.

27
00:01:19,839 --> 00:01:21,790
Security and session policy.

28
00:01:22,209 --> 00:01:25,780
Two-factor requirements, password
rules and session limits.

29
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,390
Require two-factor sign-in
for administrators and review

30
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:31,029
password and session rules.

31
00:01:31,199 --> 00:01:33,040
Single sign-on and provisioning.

32
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:37,080
Let members sign in through your
identity provider, with optional

33
00:01:37,109 --> 00:01:38,689
automatic account provisioning.

34
00:01:39,199 --> 00:01:42,710
Know your department address and
time zone, and choose at least two

35
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:44,639
people who will administer Rez grid.

36
00:01:44,909 --> 00:01:45,829
Audit history.

37
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:48,649
See who changed department
settings and when.

38
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:52,729
Know your department address and
time zone, and choose at least two

39
00:01:52,729 --> 00:01:54,699
people who will administer Rez grid.

40
00:01:54,989 --> 00:01:56,729
Account sessions and recovery.

41
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:00,849
Your own sign-in sessions,
password and two-factor settings.

42
00:02:01,309 --> 00:02:04,909
Know your department address and
time zone, and choose at least two

43
00:02:04,909 --> 00:02:06,899
people who will administer Rez grid.

44
00:02:07,119 --> 00:02:08,659
Setup help and support.

45
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:12,159
Setup Wizard, Setup
Report and Admin Assist.

46
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:16,149
Know your department address and
time zone, and choose at least two

47
00:02:16,149 --> 00:02:18,130
people who will administer Rez grid.

48
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:22,559
Passkeys add a device-backed sign-in
factor and need deliberate naming,

49
00:02:22,729 --> 00:02:24,749
removal, and recovery handling.

50
00:02:25,289 --> 00:02:28,570
Enroll from account security
on a compatible demo device.

51
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:32,309
Name the credential and review
the remaining recovery factors.

52
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:35,789
Confirm an actual sign-in
and check the credential list

53
00:02:35,830 --> 00:02:37,309
after a controlled removal.

54
00:02:37,770 --> 00:02:40,529
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

55
00:02:40,529 --> 00:02:41,979
recording the live workflow.

56
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,910
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

57
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,019
Step 1.

58
00:02:46,520 --> 00:02:48,969
Confirm the department
address and time zone.

59
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:50,140
Step 2.

60
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:54,090
Choose the modules the department
will use and review permissions.

61
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:55,290
Step 3.

62
00:02:55,750 --> 00:03:00,539
Enroll two administrators in MFA before
reviewing enforcement and recovery.

63
00:03:00,759 --> 00:03:02,279
Now verify the result.

64
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:06,020
Use separate administrator and
member accounts to check allowed

65
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:08,020
actions and resource visibility.

66
00:03:08,419 --> 00:03:11,839
Test recovery before enforcing
stricter sign-in rules.

67
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:15,829
A common problem to watch
for: Hiding a module is not

68
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:18,199
evidence that API access stops.

69
00:03:18,599 --> 00:03:22,459
MFA enrollment is separate from a
tested factor and recovery path.

70
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:24,260
Your practice task is simple.

71
00:03:24,699 --> 00:03:29,219
Complete Setup Wizard, save on each
owning screen, then Verify again.

72
00:03:29,679 --> 00:03:32,890
Keep unknown checks visible
and assign follow-up owners.

73
00:03:33,289 --> 00:03:37,070
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

74
00:03:37,530 --> 00:03:40,939
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
